1
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:12,100
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,633 --> 00:00:33,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,233
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,267 --> 00:00:41,267
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,433 --> 00:00:44,200
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,433
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,433 --> 00:00:46,867
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,867 --> 00:00:48,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,267 --> 00:00:51,233
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,633 --> 00:00:53,867
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,867 --> 00:00:55,400
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,767 --> 00:00:58,267
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,267 --> 00:01:00,400
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,267 --> 00:01:03,333
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,333 --> 00:01:06,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,367 --> 00:01:09,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:11,900
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:13,300
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:14,633
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,867 --> 00:01:20,900
<i>This is all we earned
last night?</i>

21
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:22,300
<i> Betchay, we have no customers!</i>

22
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:26,167
<i>I have to find a way
for BeerGin to earn!</i>

23
00:01:26,167 --> 00:01:28,200
<i>Everyone! Two people came
to our house.</i>

24
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:29,300
<i>They wanted Papa
to sign a document.</i>

25
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:30,633
<i>That's why they gave us
5,000 pesos!</i>

26
00:01:30,633 --> 00:01:33,300
<i> They'll make Mister Rudy
</i>our community's representative.

27
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:35,800
I will never sell our community!

28
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:38,867
<i>We just have to be prepared
for whatever happens.</i>

29
00:01:38,867 --> 00:01:40,167
<i>- Who's that?
- He works for me.</i>

30
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:41,267
<i> He's my backup plan, boss.</i>

31
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:43,200
<i>- Hurry!
- Get in!</i>

32
00:01:44,733 --> 00:01:45,900
<i> The gold is here.</i>

33
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:47,600
<i>- Sir, we've got company!
- Get them!</i>

34
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:48,800
<i> You two, cover me!</i>

35
00:01:50,333 --> 00:01:57,233
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [POLICE SIRENS BLARING]

36
00:01:58,233 --> 00:02:00,200
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [BULLETS RICOCHET]

37
00:02:01,833 --> 00:02:02,867
[GUNSHOTS]

38
00:02:02,867 --> 00:02:06,167
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECH]

39
00:02:06,167 --> 00:02:11,300
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [POLICE SIRENS BLARING]

40
00:02:12,833 --> 00:02:15,400
[GUNSHOTS]

41
00:02:15,433 --> 00:02:22,433
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

42
00:02:22,433 --> 00:02:23,900
[POLICE SIRENS BLARING]

43
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:29,933
[ENGINE REVVING]

44
00:02:29,933 --> 00:02:36,300
- [POLICE SIRENS BLARING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

45
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:40,533
[POLICE SIRENS BLARING]

46
00:02:40,533 --> 00:02:47,500
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

47
00:02:48,333 --> 00:02:50,633
- [MOTORCYCLE HORN BEEPS]
- [ENGINE REVVING]

48
00:02:51,933 --> 00:02:53,000
[MOTORCYCLE HORN BEEPS]

49
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,633
[PEOPLE SCREAMING]

50
00:02:56,633 --> 00:03:03,600
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

51
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:11,367
[COVER RUSTLING]

52
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:19,400
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

53
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:20,933
[DOG BARKING]

54
00:03:20,967 --> 00:03:22,667
[COP] Move! Step aside!

55
00:03:25,367 --> 00:03:32,333
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

56
00:03:33,833 --> 00:03:34,800
Let's go!

57
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:35,967
[DOG BARKING]

58
00:03:38,533 --> 00:03:44,567
[DOGS BARKING]

59
00:03:46,967 --> 00:03:51,033
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

60
00:03:51,033 --> 00:03:52,933
[DJANGO CHUCKLING]

61
00:03:52,933 --> 00:03:57,633
[POLICE SIRENS BLARING]

62
00:03:58,633 --> 00:03:59,900
So, did you catch him?

63
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:01,400
They're chasing him inside, sir!

64
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:03,000
Then what are you doing here?
Why aren't you inside?

65
00:04:06,367 --> 00:04:08,033
Sir, he escaped!

66
00:04:08,033 --> 00:04:09,033
You didn't catch him?

67
00:04:09,033 --> 00:04:10,800
He drove his motorcycle
too fast.

68
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:13,033
He knows the ins and outs
of Ginintuang Lupa.

69
00:04:13,033 --> 00:04:15,700
[UMALI]
Just admit that you're useless!

70
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:18,467
Check the CCTV
in the safe house, understand?

71
00:04:18,467 --> 00:04:19,633
- Go!
- Yes, sir.

72
00:04:19,633 --> 00:04:21,567
- Let's go.
- Santos, come with me.

73
00:04:21,567 --> 00:04:22,867
Where to, sir?

74
00:04:22,867 --> 00:04:25,367
I want to check
if my suspicions are correct.

75
00:04:29,067 --> 00:04:31,833
[INDISTINCT MURMUR]

76
00:04:31,833 --> 00:04:33,367
[RUDY] Alright, alright.

77
00:04:33,367 --> 00:04:36,500
For now, go home,
get some rest,

78
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:40,600
and don't forget
everything Gloria said.

79
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:42,067
- Yes.
- Get going now.

80
00:04:42,067 --> 00:04:47,733
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

81
00:04:47,733 --> 00:04:49,367
[NEIGHBOR 1] Thank you, Gloria!

82
00:04:49,367 --> 00:04:51,667
[BERTA]
Gloria! Here's your barbecue.

83
00:04:51,667 --> 00:04:52,767
I've finished cooking it
a while ago.

84
00:04:52,767 --> 00:04:54,667
And it's free, too.

85
00:04:54,667 --> 00:04:57,000
It's my thanks to you and Gabo
for helping us.

86
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:57,900
Thank you.

87
00:04:58,833 --> 00:04:59,800
I'll get going.

88
00:05:00,867 --> 00:05:02,700
Uh, love.

89
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:05,567
Uh, I think
you better prepare that,

90
00:05:05,567 --> 00:05:07,833
so we can eat dinner.

91
00:05:09,633 --> 00:05:11,100
I'll go inside first.

92
00:05:14,467 --> 00:05:21,500
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

93
00:05:26,467 --> 00:05:28,667
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

94
00:05:29,967 --> 00:05:31,667
[PLATES CLATTERING]

95
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:35,133
[OBJECTS THUD]

96
00:05:36,767 --> 00:05:41,133
Aren't you curious why Gloria
seems to know so much?

97
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:44,633
Yeah.
It's like Gloria is a genius.

98
00:05:44,633 --> 00:05:47,567
And, Gabo, it's like she knows
what she's saying.

99
00:05:47,567 --> 00:05:54,000
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

100
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,800
- [UMALI] Paquito!
- [MATET] Oh, no!

101
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:58,533
- [UMALI] Paquito!
- Ibyang! Ibyang!

102
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:00,933
NLEA! They're here.

103
00:06:00,933 --> 00:06:01,900
[UMALI] Paquito!

104
00:06:02,933 --> 00:06:04,900
Hey. Where's Paquito?

105
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:06,567
- Stop it. Uh--
- He's there, right?

106
00:06:06,567 --> 00:06:08,800
Umali. Umali!

107
00:06:09,833 --> 00:06:13,133
- Why are you here? Why?
- Where's your son?

108
00:06:13,133 --> 00:06:14,800
I just want
to confirm something.

109
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:17,767
[SANTOS] What about you, Romy?
Do you know where Django is?

110
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,867
[PAQUITO] I just asked him
to buy some booze.

111
00:06:20,867 --> 00:06:22,600
He'll be here in a while.

112
00:06:23,433 --> 00:06:25,800
- Why are you looking for me?
- [PAQUITO] There he is.

113
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:29,600
- Where'd you go?
- I haven't left this place.

114
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:31,667
Can't you smell the scum
on my body?

115
00:06:32,867 --> 00:06:34,167
What do you even want from me?

116
00:06:35,467 --> 00:06:36,933
I'm just confirming something.

117
00:06:36,933 --> 00:06:38,400
I'm just making sure...

118
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:40,833
...you're not stabbing me
in the back.

119
00:06:42,967 --> 00:06:46,200
We're chasing a criminal.
He entered Ginintuang Lupa.

120
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:47,933
Maybe you've seen him?
He's driving a motorcycle.

121
00:06:49,967 --> 00:06:52,000
Did you see his face?
What does he look like?

122
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,733
That's exactly
what I'm trying to confirm.

123
00:06:53,733 --> 00:06:54,867
Is that so?

124
00:06:54,867 --> 00:06:57,167
And yet you just barge
into our territory.

125
00:06:57,167 --> 00:06:59,633
- What, want me to beat you up?
- [UMALI] What do you want?!

126
00:06:59,633 --> 00:07:00,900
- Wait!
- [IBYANG] Wait a second!

127
00:07:00,900 --> 00:07:03,667
Wait! Django! Umali!

128
00:07:03,667 --> 00:07:07,133
We have no idea
who you're looking for!

129
00:07:07,133 --> 00:07:10,033
Next time,
make sure you're certain.

130
00:07:10,733 --> 00:07:12,133
And then you come here.

131
00:07:12,133 --> 00:07:14,833
I'll bring you that man myself!

132
00:07:14,867 --> 00:07:21,067
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

133
00:07:21,067 --> 00:07:22,133
Move out!

134
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:27,067
Move!

135
00:07:30,033 --> 00:07:30,967
So?

136
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:33,033
Did you succeed?

137
00:07:34,233 --> 00:07:36,733
Let's see
if Gabo can escape this

138
00:07:36,733 --> 00:07:39,067
now that NLEA's after him.

139
00:07:39,067 --> 00:07:41,700
[CHUCKLING]

140
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:43,800
You're really
something else, Django.

141
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:47,033
- [CLICKS TONGUE]
- [CHUCKLING]

142
00:07:47,033 --> 00:07:51,567
[PAQUITO] Django, did you get
what the Zafras needed?

143
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:54,200
Yes, Pa.
But I'm not done yet.

144
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:56,100
I'll pay them a visit again.

145
00:07:57,733 --> 00:07:59,200
[LINE RINGING]

146
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:01,867
Galo, come back and fetch me.

147
00:08:01,867 --> 00:08:03,867
We can't let that Lucas
beat us.

148
00:08:03,867 --> 00:08:04,833
Hurry up.

149
00:08:05,300 --> 00:08:06,500
Where's my vest?

150
00:08:07,867 --> 00:08:09,000
Here, boss.

151
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:12,067
Pa. I'll get going.

152
00:08:16,767 --> 00:08:18,000
I'm getting nervous, Pa.

153
00:08:20,033 --> 00:08:22,033
She might be starting
to regain her memories.

154
00:08:24,567 --> 00:08:27,667
[MAMENG] Well, what if
her memories do come back?

155
00:08:27,667 --> 00:08:29,333
What are we going to do?

156
00:08:29,333 --> 00:08:31,100
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

157
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:33,933
[PLASTIC BAG RUSTLING]

158
00:08:37,733 --> 00:08:39,167
There's nothing we can do,
Auntie...

159
00:08:39,167 --> 00:08:42,167
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

160
00:08:42,167 --> 00:08:43,867
...but tell her the truth.

161
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,567
That we just did that...

162
00:08:48,567 --> 00:08:51,000
[MUSIC TURNS STIRRING]

163
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,800
...to save her life.

164
00:08:53,767 --> 00:08:59,200
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

165
00:09:01,533 --> 00:09:04,967
- [MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [CARS APPROACHING]

166
00:09:04,967 --> 00:09:06,167
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

167
00:09:07,467 --> 00:09:08,633
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

168
00:09:10,167 --> 00:09:11,633
Bring 'em in.

169
00:09:17,667 --> 00:09:18,667
[CHEST BOX THUDS]

170
00:09:21,967 --> 00:09:23,000
[CHEST BOX THUDS]

171
00:09:32,667 --> 00:09:35,900
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

172
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:37,933
[MARIANO, DEBORAH CHUCKLE]

173
00:09:51,833 --> 00:09:52,800
Nice work!

174
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:54,667
Good job, son!

175
00:09:54,667 --> 00:09:56,800
[MARIANO, DEBORAH CLAPS]

176
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:58,767
Boss Lucas
is really something else.

177
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:00,900
If it weren't for him,

178
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:02,833
we wouldn't get
the gold bars back!

179
00:10:02,867 --> 00:10:04,533
- Right?! [LAUGHS MOCKINGLY]
- [MEN CHEER, CLAP]

180
00:10:04,533 --> 00:10:05,600
Just great!

181
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:07,733
- [CHEERING, APPLAUSE CONTINUES]
- Amazing!

182
00:10:07,733 --> 00:10:08,833
[DJANGO CHUCKLES MOCKINGLY]

183
00:10:09,733 --> 00:10:12,067
- Arturo.
- Why, sir?

184
00:10:12,067 --> 00:10:14,433
Ask them
to bring out some drinks.

185
00:10:14,433 --> 00:10:15,900
This calls for a celebration.

186
00:10:15,900 --> 00:10:17,067
Yeah!

187
00:10:17,067 --> 00:10:18,533
[MEN CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

188
00:10:18,533 --> 00:10:19,733
It's time for happy hour!

189
00:10:19,733 --> 00:10:21,667
[DJANGO LAUGHING]

190
00:10:21,667 --> 00:10:25,567
[MEN CHANTING]
Lucas! Lucas! Lucas!

191
00:10:25,567 --> 00:10:26,567
Boss.

192
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:34,867
Well then,

193
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:35,900
put those away.

194
00:10:38,967 --> 00:10:42,067
[MEN CHANTING]
Lucas! Lucas! Lucas!

195
00:10:42,067 --> 00:10:44,033
Why haven't you
thrown that out?!

196
00:10:44,033 --> 00:10:46,633
You're not done cleaning yet?!

197
00:10:46,633 --> 00:10:48,933
I've already told you
to change the bulbs!

198
00:10:48,933 --> 00:10:49,933
They're too old!

199
00:10:49,933 --> 00:10:51,233
And remove those!

200
00:10:51,233 --> 00:10:54,100
It's making the space
look cluttered!

201
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:56,467
[ROSANNA]
Hold on, I'll deal with her.

202
00:10:56,467 --> 00:10:58,100
Hey! Betchay!

203
00:10:58,100 --> 00:10:59,967
Nothing needs changing in here!

204
00:10:59,967 --> 00:11:02,933
We can't just spend
on redecorating!

205
00:11:03,767 --> 00:11:05,867
I'm not trying to change it.

206
00:11:05,867 --> 00:11:08,100
I just want the space
to look better.

207
00:11:08,133 --> 00:11:11,767
I want our patrons to have
something pretty to look at.

208
00:11:11,767 --> 00:11:15,467
Come on, ladies,

209
00:11:15,467 --> 00:11:17,633
do you really think
you'll be able to bring in men?

210
00:11:17,633 --> 00:11:20,633
You've only been the manager
for a few days, Betchay.

211
00:11:20,633 --> 00:11:22,800
And now you think
so highly of yourself.

212
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:24,600
Of course.

213
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:27,567
Matter of fact, ever since
I became the manager,

214
00:11:27,567 --> 00:11:30,133
I've brought in more money
here at BeerGin.

215
00:11:30,133 --> 00:11:32,900
And this bar
will be more profitable

216
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:35,633
when you're not
the escorts anymore!

217
00:11:35,633 --> 00:11:37,067
What do you mean?

218
00:11:37,067 --> 00:11:39,067
- Are you going to replace us?
- Hmm...

219
00:11:39,067 --> 00:11:41,633
Hey, hey, hey,
you can't just kick us out

220
00:11:41,667 --> 00:11:43,267
because we've been
working here for so long.

221
00:11:43,267 --> 00:11:44,500
Hey, hey, hey,

222
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:47,167
I can do whatever I want.

223
00:11:47,167 --> 00:11:50,867
Because I only want
the best for BeerGin.

224
00:11:50,867 --> 00:11:53,000
The first order of business

225
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,767
is laying you all off.

226
00:11:55,767 --> 00:11:57,500
Look at yourselves, ladies!

227
00:11:57,500 --> 00:12:00,100
With your wrinkly skin
and calloused hands!

228
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:01,800
This bar is old,

229
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:04,000
and the escorts
are old hags too!

230
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,033
- Watch your mouth!
- Especially you!

231
00:12:06,033 --> 00:12:09,600
You look like you're
knocking on heaven's door!

232
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:11,200
Heaven's door, she said?

233
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:12,600
Really, huh?!

234
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:15,867
- [BETCHAY SHRIEKING]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

235
00:12:15,900 --> 00:12:18,033
[OBJECTS THUD]

236
00:12:18,033 --> 00:12:20,667
Really, huh?! You witch!

237
00:12:20,667 --> 00:12:23,000
- Stop it!
- [ROSANNA] Shameless witch!

238
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,533
[BLOWS LANDING]

239
00:12:25,533 --> 00:12:27,000
Hey! Stop them!

240
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,033
- [BETCHAY] Ouch!
- You asked for this!

241
00:12:29,033 --> 00:12:32,000
- Argh! Stop it!
- [BLOWS LANDING]

242
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,867
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [WOMEN SHRIEK]

243
00:12:33,867 --> 00:12:34,900
That's enough!

244
00:12:34,900 --> 00:12:37,333
What the hell
is happening here?!

245
00:12:37,333 --> 00:12:39,133
[BETCHAY CRYING]

246
00:12:39,133 --> 00:12:41,033
Paquito!

247
00:12:41,033 --> 00:12:44,133
They attacked me!
I didn't even do anything!

248
00:12:44,133 --> 00:12:47,033
- [ROSANNA] Liar!
- Don't hurt Betchay!

249
00:12:47,033 --> 00:12:50,033
If you hurt her again,
you'll have to face me instead!

250
00:12:50,067 --> 00:12:52,867
Everyone who'll go
against Betchay

251
00:12:52,867 --> 00:12:54,900
is going against me too!

252
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:57,733
- Get out! All of you!
- Get out!

253
00:12:57,733 --> 00:12:59,200
You can't kick me out!

254
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:01,833
I built this bar!

255
00:13:01,833 --> 00:13:03,033
Rosanna!

256
00:13:03,033 --> 00:13:04,233
You owed me money!

257
00:13:04,233 --> 00:13:06,900
BeerGin is all mine now!

258
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:08,233
Get out of here!

259
00:13:08,233 --> 00:13:10,733
Don't show
your face here ever again!

260
00:13:10,733 --> 00:13:14,033
Boss, we've been
working for so long!

261
00:13:14,033 --> 00:13:16,867
We've nowhere else to go! [SOBS]

262
00:13:16,867 --> 00:13:19,233
Boss, we're begging you!

263
00:13:19,233 --> 00:13:22,033
Please, we're begging you!

264
00:13:22,067 --> 00:13:23,767
This won't happen again!

265
00:13:23,767 --> 00:13:26,900
Please forgive us!
We're begging you!

266
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:28,867
We'll be good, boss! [CRYING]

267
00:13:28,867 --> 00:13:30,800
We'll be good, I swear!

268
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:33,800
You're all just charity cases!
Get out of here!

269
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:36,767
Oh, didn't you hear her?
Throw them out!

270
00:13:36,767 --> 00:13:38,400
[MEN] Get out! Get out!

271
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:41,400
- We're begging you, boss!
- Get out! Move!

272
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:43,233
- Boss!
- Shut it!

273
00:13:43,233 --> 00:13:46,033
- Get out!
- I said move!

274
00:13:46,033 --> 00:13:47,400
- Get out of here!
- Out!

275
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:48,633
Move faster!

276
00:13:48,633 --> 00:13:51,067
[WOMEN SOBBING]

277
00:13:51,067 --> 00:13:53,067
Get out!

278
00:13:53,067 --> 00:13:54,000
[MUSIC FADES]

279
00:13:55,633 --> 00:13:58,800
[UTENSIL CLANKING]

280
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:05,767
[SULLEN MUSIC PLAYING]

281
00:14:06,833 --> 00:14:07,933
Come on.

282
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:09,800
Let's eat.

283
00:14:29,267 --> 00:14:30,233
Uh...

284
00:14:31,833 --> 00:14:32,800
Gloria.

285
00:14:33,367 --> 00:14:35,300
Do you remember
where you lived?

286
00:14:39,333 --> 00:14:41,067
Uh...

287
00:14:42,100 --> 00:14:44,267
I-I don't remember.

288
00:14:45,100 --> 00:14:48,067
Maybe Gabo knows.
Do you know where I lived?

289
00:14:54,333 --> 00:14:56,300
In...

290
00:14:59,033 --> 00:15:00,333
...in Palawan.

291
00:15:00,333 --> 00:15:01,633
In...

292
00:15:02,333 --> 00:15:04,100
in San Vicente.

293
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:06,967
Oh.

294
00:15:06,967 --> 00:15:08,767
So that's where I'm from.

295
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:11,833
Who are your parents?

296
00:15:16,067 --> 00:15:17,700
[STAMMERS]

297
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:19,667
Gabo, have you met them?

298
00:15:21,700 --> 00:15:24,000
Uh, love...

299
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:29,167
Ever since we met
and got married,

300
00:15:29,167 --> 00:15:34,033
you haven't mentioned
a thing about your parents.

301
00:15:34,867 --> 00:15:40,200
Not once did I see someone
visit you in jail.

302
00:15:40,200 --> 00:15:42,333
I don't know
who your parents are.

303
00:15:44,900 --> 00:15:46,433
What a shame.

304
00:15:46,433 --> 00:15:50,033
Does that mean you were
living alone here in Manila?

305
00:15:53,767 --> 00:15:54,733
Gloria.

306
00:15:55,933 --> 00:15:59,667
We just want
to ask you something.

307
00:16:01,333 --> 00:16:03,900
Do you remember anything...

308
00:16:06,833 --> 00:16:08,000
about your past

309
00:16:09,433 --> 00:16:10,933
and who you really are?

310
00:16:10,933 --> 00:16:13,700
[MUSIC TURNS SUSPENSEFUL]

311
00:16:15,567 --> 00:16:18,700
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

312
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:19,667
Nope.

313
00:16:20,700 --> 00:16:22,267
A-Are you sure?

314
00:16:23,033 --> 00:16:24,000
[STAMMERS]

315
00:16:24,067 --> 00:16:27,700
Because earlier, we noticed...

316
00:16:28,567 --> 00:16:31,000
that you sounded confident
when you said all that.

317
00:16:32,133 --> 00:16:36,267
We couldn't believe everything
that came out of your mouth.

318
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:38,567
E-Earlier?

319
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:41,533
Honestly, I don't even know.

320
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:42,933
It just...

321
00:16:42,967 --> 00:16:45,500
It just popped
into my head somehow.

322
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:47,033
I don't know.

323
00:16:47,733 --> 00:16:50,333
We thought maybe it was...

324
00:16:50,333 --> 00:16:52,133
the start of your memories
coming back.

325
00:16:52,133 --> 00:16:53,467
[MAMENG] That's true.

326
00:16:53,467 --> 00:16:56,400
You were so amazing back there.

327
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:59,400
It was like you had
all the laws memorized.

328
00:16:59,400 --> 00:17:01,300
You sounded so smart.

329
00:17:01,300 --> 00:17:02,400
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

330
00:17:02,933 --> 00:17:03,900
[GABO] Gloria...

331
00:17:03,967 --> 00:17:05,167
Love...

332
00:17:05,167 --> 00:17:06,433
Are you sure?

333
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:09,533
We were worried, you know.

334
00:17:11,133 --> 00:17:15,433
We were really surprised
by everything you said.

335
00:17:16,500 --> 00:17:17,600
[SAM] Oh...

336
00:17:17,600 --> 00:17:18,967
I don't remember any of it.

337
00:17:18,967 --> 00:17:19,967
Did I...

338
00:17:19,967 --> 00:17:21,200
Did I say something wrong?

339
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:23,200
- No, not at all.
- [RUDY] Absolutely not.

340
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:26,167
Everything you said was right.

341
00:17:26,167 --> 00:17:28,867
That's why we're all grateful.

342
00:17:28,867 --> 00:17:33,933
You've been helping us,
and even our neighbors too.

343
00:17:34,467 --> 00:17:35,500
Mm.
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

344
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:37,267
I just really want to help.

345
00:17:37,267 --> 00:17:39,867
Well then, that's settled...

346
00:17:39,867 --> 00:17:41,933
- Pa, let's eat.
- Dinner's waiting.

347
00:17:41,933 --> 00:17:43,600
- Come on.
- Sit down, Gabo.

348
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,600
- [CHAIRS RATTLING]
- [GABO, SAM CHUCKLE]

349
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:47,167
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

350
00:17:47,167 --> 00:17:49,533
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

351
00:17:49,567 --> 00:17:51,467
Here, dig in.

352
00:17:51,467 --> 00:17:53,633
- Go on.
- Let's eat.

353
00:17:53,633 --> 00:17:55,600
- Pa...
- This is for you both.

354
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:58,167
- Here's to my son, Lucas!
- Cheers!

355
00:17:58,167 --> 00:17:59,900
- Cheers!
- To Lucas!

356
00:17:59,900 --> 00:18:01,900
- This is for you, boss!
- Cheers!

357
00:18:01,900 --> 00:18:03,967
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER, LAUGHTER]
- [GLASSES CLINK]

358
00:18:03,967 --> 00:18:04,967
[DJANGO] So good!

359
00:18:04,967 --> 00:18:06,200
[LAUGHTER]

360
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:08,000
- This stuff is sick!
- [EXHALES LOUDLY]

361
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,833
[LAUGHTER, WHOOPING]

362
00:18:09,833 --> 00:18:11,867
[ARTURO]
Here's Django's part, sir.

363
00:18:11,867 --> 00:18:15,000
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER
IN DISTANCE]

364
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:19,900
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

365
00:18:19,900 --> 00:18:21,567
- [DJANGO] Boss.
- I have to make a call.

366
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,067
[CHEERING IN DISTANCE]

367
00:18:23,067 --> 00:18:24,400
Boss.

368
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:25,933
This is your side of the deal.

369
00:18:25,933 --> 00:18:27,200
[DEBORAH] Enjoy yourself!

370
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:28,167
- It's your night!
- Two hundred thousand pesos.

371
00:18:28,167 --> 00:18:29,933
[CHEERING, LAUGHTER]

372
00:18:29,933 --> 00:18:31,867
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

373
00:18:31,867 --> 00:18:34,000
This is dope, boss!
[CHUCKLES] Thank you.

374
00:18:34,667 --> 00:18:36,600
[DJANGO LAUGHS]

375
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:39,167
I made the right decision
to hire you.

376
00:18:39,167 --> 00:18:41,167
You're even better
than your father.

377
00:18:41,167 --> 00:18:42,933
I just take after him.

378
00:18:42,933 --> 00:18:45,100
But I'm younger, and faster.

379
00:18:45,100 --> 00:18:46,433
[LAUGHS]

380
00:18:46,433 --> 00:18:47,933
Come on, cheers!

381
00:18:47,933 --> 00:18:49,533
- Let's toast to that!
- Cheers!

382
00:18:49,533 --> 00:18:51,500
- Cheers, boss!
- Boss!

383
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:54,067
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]

384
00:18:54,067 --> 00:18:55,967
[MARIANO] So, what kind of bonus
do you want?

385
00:18:56,267 --> 00:18:57,400
[DJANGO CHUCKLES]

386
00:18:57,967 --> 00:18:59,433
[GLASSES THUD]

387
00:18:59,433 --> 00:19:01,233
That one, boss.
[CHUCKLES]

388
00:19:01,233 --> 00:19:03,067
I've been eyeing it
all night long.

389
00:19:03,067 --> 00:19:04,167
It looks nice.

390
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:06,400
- [GALO] Yeah, it's lit.
- What, this one?

391
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:07,600
That's the one, boss.
[CHUCKLES]

392
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:08,600
[SCOFFS]

393
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:10,867
I'm impressed by your guts.

394
00:19:11,533 --> 00:19:13,933
Of all things, you're after
my gold necklace.

395
00:19:13,933 --> 00:19:15,133
[DJANGO LAUGHS]

396
00:19:15,133 --> 00:19:16,600
I've got guts, boss.

397
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:18,033
And I bet rocking that one
would feel amazing.

398
00:19:18,033 --> 00:19:20,567
[LAUGHTER]

399
00:19:20,567 --> 00:19:22,067
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]
- [GLASSES CLINK]

400
00:19:22,067 --> 00:19:23,100
[SCOFFS]

401
00:19:23,100 --> 00:19:25,567
- Here we go! Whoo!
- It's happening!

402
00:19:25,567 --> 00:19:27,067
- Alright then.
- Nice!

403
00:19:27,067 --> 00:19:28,267
It's yours.

404
00:19:28,300 --> 00:19:29,933
[CHEERING, CLAPPING]

405
00:19:29,933 --> 00:19:31,600
- That's fire!
- I used to rock silver.

406
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:34,600
But hey, gold suits me better!
[LAUGHTER]

407
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:36,567
- Looks good on you, dude!
- Cheers, boss!

408
00:19:36,567 --> 00:19:38,400
- Let's drink, boss!
- Raise a glass!

409
00:19:39,167 --> 00:19:40,567
[DJANGO] Listen, boss.

410
00:19:40,567 --> 00:19:43,600
If you need me again,
I'm just one call away.

411
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:45,000
You know that.

412
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:46,333
I'm easy to talk to.

413
00:19:46,333 --> 00:19:47,600
I'm your guy.

414
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:49,100
[LAUGHTER]

415
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:50,467
Very good!

416
00:19:50,467 --> 00:19:51,467
[CHUCKLES]

417
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:53,567
[LAUGHTER]

418
00:19:54,000 --> 00:20:00,967
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

419
00:20:02,633 --> 00:20:04,333
- [BETCHAY] Boss...
- What's up?

420
00:20:05,033 --> 00:20:06,700
Thank you.

421
00:20:06,700 --> 00:20:09,133
For having my back
in front of them.

422
00:20:09,133 --> 00:20:12,367
You still don't believe me,
Betchay?

423
00:20:12,367 --> 00:20:16,000
Didn't I tell you that I was
going to make you a queen

424
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:18,433
and put you on a pedestal?

425
00:20:18,433 --> 00:20:22,000
And if anyone ever crosses you,
they'll have me as their enemy.

426
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,467
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

427
00:20:23,467 --> 00:20:25,667
It's just that
I'm not used to...

428
00:20:25,667 --> 00:20:29,500
being the one protected,
with my welfare put first.

429
00:20:30,033 --> 00:20:33,100
So this is what it feels like
to be... [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

430
00:20:33,100 --> 00:20:34,500
...valued.

431
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:36,967
I'm serious about you, Betchay.

432
00:20:37,333 --> 00:20:39,500
I'm going to do more than that.

433
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:42,533
I'm ready to kill for you!

434
00:20:43,333 --> 00:20:46,633
That's how Paquito loves,
Betchay!

435
00:20:46,633 --> 00:20:48,667
And that's why I'm the biggest
PaqBet supporter!

436
00:20:48,667 --> 00:20:49,733
- Huh?
- "PaqBet"?

437
00:20:49,733 --> 00:20:51,300
Paquito, Betchay...

438
00:20:51,300 --> 00:20:53,333
When you put them together...
PaqBet!

439
00:20:53,333 --> 00:20:54,700
- Genius, right?
- [SILLY MUSIC PLAYING]

440
00:20:54,700 --> 00:20:56,400
- Uh, boss...
- PaqBet!

441
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:57,667
- Oh?
- Uh...

442
00:20:57,667 --> 00:20:59,667
I was in the right,
don't you agree?

443
00:20:59,667 --> 00:21:02,667
All I want is for BeerGin
to make a profit.

444
00:21:02,667 --> 00:21:04,233
Of course.

445
00:21:04,233 --> 00:21:08,000
Whatever you want to do,
it will be done.

446
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,500
You're the queen here.

447
00:21:09,533 --> 00:21:10,600
I don't want to be a queen.

448
00:21:10,600 --> 00:21:12,200
Being a princess is
more my thing.

449
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:14,433
Alright then,
you're the princess now.

450
00:21:14,433 --> 00:21:15,700
- Come on.
- Really?

451
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:17,100
- Let's drink.
- Jack! Jill!

452
00:21:17,100 --> 00:21:18,400
Yes, ma'am? What is it?

453
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:22,100
Find a signboard and put
"Wanted: Female Entertainer."

454
00:21:22,100 --> 00:21:23,400
We'll post it outside.

455
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:26,200
Call all the women
in your lives.

456
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:28,100
Your girlfriends,
even your daughters!

457
00:21:28,100 --> 00:21:30,333
Life is tough,
we need to work!

458
00:21:30,333 --> 00:21:32,267
- So hurry up!
- Pretty ladies coming right up!

459
00:21:32,267 --> 00:21:34,767
At last, I'll have my favorite
at BeerGin!

460
00:21:34,767 --> 00:21:36,333
[SLOW MUSIC PLAYING
OVER SPEAKERS]

461
00:21:36,333 --> 00:21:39,067
Princess Betchay.
[EXHALES LOUDLY]

462
00:21:39,067 --> 00:21:41,733
- My PaqBet in life.
- [GIGGLES]

463
00:21:41,767 --> 00:21:43,533
There we go!
[CHUCKLES]

464
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:46,367
[GLASSES THUD]

465
00:21:47,300 --> 00:21:48,400
Arturo.

466
00:21:48,400 --> 00:21:49,433
[ALCOHOL SLOSHING]

467
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:51,200
We're good now.
Take us home.

468
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:52,400
[LAUGHTER]

469
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:53,767
Follow me.

470
00:21:57,300 --> 00:21:58,733
My friends!

471
00:21:58,733 --> 00:22:00,100
We'll be on our way.

472
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:01,700
- [DJANGO LAUGHS]
- [INDSTINCT SHOUTING]

473
00:22:02,133 --> 00:22:04,100
[CAR DOOR SLIDING

474
00:22:05,267 --> 00:22:06,267
[LUCAS] Wait!

475
00:22:09,100 --> 00:22:12,133
Before you forget,
you all need to wear this.

476
00:22:12,133 --> 00:22:16,633
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

477
00:22:16,667 --> 00:22:18,233
Is that still necessary, boss?

478
00:22:20,100 --> 00:22:22,233
You've only done one job.

479
00:22:22,233 --> 00:22:25,267
That doesn't mean
you're one of us.

480
00:22:25,267 --> 00:22:27,733
And no matter how many times
Dad calls for you,

481
00:22:28,833 --> 00:22:30,767
whenever we're on a mission,

482
00:22:30,767 --> 00:22:32,100
I call the shots.

483
00:22:32,433 --> 00:22:33,600
Absolutely.

484
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:35,800
I've got nothing to prove
to you, anyway.

485
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:37,767
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

486
00:22:37,767 --> 00:22:38,800
Boss.

487
00:22:40,133 --> 00:22:41,300
[DJANGO CHUCKLES]

488
00:22:41,300 --> 00:22:44,267
Go on, blindfold them.

489
00:22:48,233 --> 00:22:49,400
I'll do it, boss.

490
00:22:49,433 --> 00:22:50,800
[ENGINE HUMMING]

491
00:22:50,800 --> 00:22:53,800
I wouldn't want Your Highness
to exhaust himself.

492
00:22:53,800 --> 00:22:56,800
[LAUGHTER]

493
00:22:56,800 --> 00:22:59,800
- Move it!
- Come on, hurry!

494
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:01,300
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

495
00:23:01,300 --> 00:23:03,133
You know where to take them.

496
00:23:03,133 --> 00:23:04,167
Yes, boss.

497
00:23:04,167 --> 00:23:05,267
[CAR DOOR SLIDING]

498
00:23:05,267 --> 00:23:10,667
[ENGINE REVVING]

499
00:23:15,633 --> 00:23:17,667
He just got lucky this one time.

500
00:23:17,667 --> 00:23:19,333
But he's no better than me.

501
00:23:19,667 --> 00:23:22,667
He is nothing compared to you.

502
00:23:22,700 --> 00:23:24,700
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

503
00:23:24,700 --> 00:23:27,767
I won't let those thugs beat us.

504
00:23:28,167 --> 00:23:30,700
[LAO] That one's flying
way too high, boss.

505
00:23:31,167 --> 00:23:32,600
He needs to be knocked down.

506
00:23:33,167 --> 00:23:34,667
Let him fly.

507
00:23:35,667 --> 00:23:38,933
It'll be sweeter when the time
comes to bring him down.

508
00:23:44,300 --> 00:23:45,000
[SING-SONG VOICE]
Here we are!

509
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:46,333
Pa!

510
00:23:46,333 --> 00:23:48,333
- [CHUCKLES]
- [PAQUITO] Django!

511
00:23:48,333 --> 00:23:49,533
They're back.

512
00:23:49,533 --> 00:23:51,000
Mission accomplished.

513
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:52,500
[PAQUITO LAUGHS]

514
00:23:52,500 --> 00:23:54,067
[EXCLAIMING, CLAPPING]

515
00:23:54,067 --> 00:23:55,500
How much is this?

516
00:23:56,200 --> 00:23:58,200
200,000!

517
00:23:58,200 --> 00:24:00,867
- [CACKLES]
- Wow!

518
00:24:00,867 --> 00:24:02,500
[PAQUITO] That's it, Django!

519
00:24:02,500 --> 00:24:05,733
Show them you're my son!

520
00:24:05,733 --> 00:24:09,533
Show them what you're made of!

521
00:24:09,533 --> 00:24:11,533
[CACKLING]

522
00:24:11,533 --> 00:24:15,567
This means you'll be
working for the Zafras now.

523
00:24:15,567 --> 00:24:17,533
We're just getting started.

524
00:24:17,533 --> 00:24:19,200
And here's even better news.

525
00:24:19,200 --> 00:24:21,533
If the police
start poking around,

526
00:24:21,533 --> 00:24:23,600
we won't take the fall.

527
00:24:23,600 --> 00:24:25,167
Gabo will!

528
00:24:25,167 --> 00:24:26,867
- [CACKLES]
- Nice!

529
00:24:26,867 --> 00:24:28,533
[GLASSES CLINK]

530
00:24:29,767 --> 00:24:33,233
Gabo, did you prepare an outfit
for your interview tomorrow?

531
00:24:33,233 --> 00:24:36,033
Yes. I'll just wear
my usual clothes.

532
00:24:36,033 --> 00:24:38,067
Oh, those won't do.

533
00:24:38,067 --> 00:24:41,567
You need to wear
formal clothes.

534
00:24:41,567 --> 00:24:42,467
Formal?

535
00:24:42,467 --> 00:24:43,867
Is that necessary?

536
00:24:43,867 --> 00:24:45,533
My clothes are fine.

537
00:24:46,733 --> 00:24:47,900
You know what,
leave that to me.

538
00:24:47,900 --> 00:24:49,667
Did you prepare a resume?

539
00:24:50,567 --> 00:24:51,900
What's a resume?

540
00:24:51,900 --> 00:24:55,800
It's like a bio-data form,
Gabo.

541
00:24:55,800 --> 00:24:57,933
- A bio-data form?
- Yes.

542
00:24:57,933 --> 00:24:58,933
Here's what we'll do.

543
00:24:58,933 --> 00:25:00,967
I'll buy you
a bio-data form later.

544
00:25:00,967 --> 00:25:04,767
Then, let's prepare
for your interview tomorrow.

545
00:25:04,800 --> 00:25:06,133
- [MAMENG] Oh dear.
- [GABO CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

546
00:25:06,133 --> 00:25:08,133
Gabo's got that covered.

547
00:25:08,133 --> 00:25:10,100
He's a resourceful guy.

548
00:25:10,100 --> 00:25:12,900
Auntie, my wife
hasn't seen me in action.

549
00:25:12,900 --> 00:25:15,500
- [MAMENG CHUCKLES]
- I have a way with words.

550
00:25:15,500 --> 00:25:17,833
You should've seen how
I talked to my teachers before.

551
00:25:17,833 --> 00:25:20,133
[LAUGHTER]

552
00:25:20,133 --> 00:25:22,067
By the way, Gabo,

553
00:25:22,067 --> 00:25:25,267
make sure to get a proper job.

554
00:25:25,267 --> 00:25:30,533
[DANTE] What about your
messenger job, Gabo?

555
00:25:31,933 --> 00:25:36,067
Well, if I don't get
hired tomorrow,

556
00:25:36,100 --> 00:25:40,067
then I'll have no choice
but to go back to my old job.

557
00:25:42,133 --> 00:25:46,600
Just make sure you
get a legitimate one.

558
00:25:46,600 --> 00:25:48,133
Are we clear on that?

559
00:25:48,133 --> 00:25:49,867
Of course, my love.

560
00:25:49,867 --> 00:25:54,933
I'll only accept the job
if it's an honorable one.

561
00:25:54,933 --> 00:25:59,800
I want to support my family
with clean money.

562
00:25:59,800 --> 00:26:03,300
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

563
00:26:03,300 --> 00:26:07,300
Did you get along with
Boss Mariano's son?

564
00:26:07,300 --> 00:26:08,933
Not really, Papa.

565
00:26:08,967 --> 00:26:10,167
He's a little pipsqueak!

566
00:26:10,167 --> 00:26:12,900
[LAUGHTER]

567
00:26:12,900 --> 00:26:15,200
I'm going to wipe the floor
with that kid.

568
00:26:15,200 --> 00:26:18,900
Then when they
entrust their operations to me,

569
00:26:18,900 --> 00:26:21,833
I will get everything I want.

570
00:26:21,833 --> 00:26:23,833
Money, power...

571
00:26:23,833 --> 00:26:25,833
- Yes!
- ...and the ladies!

572
00:26:25,833 --> 00:26:28,167
[LAUGHTER, CLAPPING]

573
00:26:28,167 --> 00:26:30,633
Hey, wait a minute.

574
00:26:31,333 --> 00:26:32,867
That's new.

575
00:26:32,867 --> 00:26:35,000
- It's beautiful.
- Oh, yeah.

576
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:36,667
- Is that for me?
- [CHUCKLES]

577
00:26:36,667 --> 00:26:38,000
- Hmm?
- You wanna?

578
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:40,133
- Of course.
- You wanna get hurt?

579
00:26:40,133 --> 00:26:42,333
[LAUGHS]

580
00:26:42,367 --> 00:26:46,933
I will give this
to my soon-to-be wife...

581
00:26:46,933 --> 00:26:48,000
Gloria.

582
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:49,267
[LAUGHTER]

583
00:26:49,267 --> 00:26:51,200
- Oh, boy...
- [CHUCKLES]

584
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:53,833
You liked it?
Let us see it!

585
00:26:53,833 --> 00:26:56,333
- Oh...
- It's real.

586
00:26:56,333 --> 00:26:58,200
Don't worry, Gloria.

587
00:26:58,200 --> 00:26:59,867
My son is a changed man.

588
00:26:59,867 --> 00:27:02,033
He'd never do anything
that'll put him back in jail.

589
00:27:02,033 --> 00:27:04,200
[MAMENG] That's why
he turned down the job

590
00:27:04,200 --> 00:27:07,600
Paquito and Django offered.

591
00:27:07,600 --> 00:27:10,033
He's never going back
to his old life.

592
00:27:10,033 --> 00:27:11,000
That's right.

593
00:27:11,867 --> 00:27:17,367
Love, ever since
we met in prison,

594
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:19,867
I promised myself

595
00:27:19,867 --> 00:27:22,067
I would never go back there.

596
00:27:22,067 --> 00:27:24,233
Especially now that
you've been released.

597
00:27:24,233 --> 00:27:27,800
I want us to start a family.

598
00:27:27,800 --> 00:27:31,133
I want to become a father
our child can be proud of.

599
00:27:31,133 --> 00:27:32,600
[DANTE] Wow.

600
00:27:34,200 --> 00:27:36,267
How inspiring. [CHUCKLES]

601
00:27:36,367 --> 00:27:43,267
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

602
00:27:55,567 --> 00:27:57,600
<i>I can offer you
something better.</i>

603
00:27:57,600 --> 00:27:59,100
<i> Just sign this document.</i>

604
00:27:59,100 --> 00:28:02,133
You were never a father to Sam.

605
00:28:02,133 --> 00:28:04,633
<i>I know I made mistakes
that I can never fix.</i>

606
00:28:04,633 --> 00:28:06,133
<i> Those countless days</i>

607
00:28:06,133 --> 00:28:09,167
<i>of making her feel
undeserving of your love,</i>

608
00:28:09,167 --> 00:28:11,100
<i>up until your last moment
together,</i>

609
00:28:11,100 --> 00:28:12,667
<i> that's her last memory of you!</i>

610
00:28:12,667 --> 00:28:15,667
<i>- What is your full name?
- Gabriel "Handsome" Magtibay.</i>

611
00:28:15,667 --> 00:28:18,467
<i>Show that you can
be professional.</i>

612
00:28:18,467 --> 00:28:20,500
- [GRUNTS LOUDLY]
<i> - You sound like a criminal!</i>

613
00:28:20,500 --> 00:28:21,600
<i>- Sex?
- Anytime.</i>

614
00:28:21,600 --> 00:28:22,833
<i> Act professionally.</i>

615
00:28:22,867 --> 00:28:23,867
<i> How do I do that?</i>

616
00:28:23,867 --> 00:28:25,433
<i> "Good morning."</i>

617
00:28:25,433 --> 00:28:27,633
<i>- What was your previous job?
- A thief! A burglar!</i>

618
00:28:27,633 --> 00:28:30,633
<i> Those are qualities they
</i>won't find in other applicants!

619
00:28:30,633 --> 00:28:32,833
<i>I want to have a decent job
when we have a kid.</i>

620
00:28:32,833 --> 00:28:35,633
<i> I want to support my family.</i>

621
00:28:35,633 --> 00:28:37,167
<i> Don't worry, Gabo.</i>

622
00:28:37,167 --> 00:28:39,300
<i> You have a good heart.</i>

623
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:43,333
<i>God can see
what's in our hearts.</i>

624
00:28:43,333 --> 00:28:45,300
<i>I should be using
this opportunity</i>

625
00:28:45,300 --> 00:28:46,667
<i> to find out the truth.</i>

626
00:28:46,667 --> 00:28:48,767
<i> I'm getting too close to him.</i>

627
00:28:48,767 --> 00:28:51,733
<i>I think I really want to help
and protect him now.</i>
